# Root .gitignore for the Mark-XLVIII-main / Jarvis_notes monorepo.
# Created 2026-07-25 alongside the graphify integration -- see
# Jarvis_notes/workflows/contracts-compartmentalization-and-synergy/Plan.md
# for the audit that found this repo previously had no root-level .gitignore
# at all. Subdirectory projects (Agent_backend/, ToolSet/) keep their own,
# more specific .gitignore files; this one covers the shared/root concerns.

# -----------------------------
# graphify knowledge graph output
# -----------------------------
# Regenerated by .git/hooks/post-commit on every commit (graphify update),
# and by `graphify extract` manually. Large (graph.json/graph.html run several
# MB each) and fully reproducible from source -- committing it would create a
# multi-MB diff on every single future commit for no benefit.
graphify-out/
**/graphify-out/

# -----------------------------
# Vault backups (ad-hoc safety nets, not durable history)
# -----------------------------
# e.g. Jarvis_notes_backup_2026-07-25_pre_lifecycle_migration/ -- a
# point-in-time copy taken before a risky bulk vault operation. git history
# is the durable record; these are meant to be deleted once confidence is
# established, not committed.
Jarvis_notes_backup_*/

# -----------------------------
# Python
# -----------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.pyo
*$py.class
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
.tox/
.nox/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# -----------------------------
# Obsidian community plugins
# -----------------------------
# Vendored third-party plugin code, and -- more importantly -- their data.json
# files hold live secrets. obsidian-local-rest-api stores its bearer API key
# plus the self-signed certificate AND its private key there in plaintext.
# `.obsidian/` itself is tracked for shared vault settings, so without this rule
# a broad `git add` would commit those. Plugins are installed per machine
# through the Obsidian UI; they are not repo content.
Jarvis_notes/.obsidian/plugins/

# -----------------------------
# Nested independent git repos (not submodules)
# -----------------------------
# These are separate projects that happen to live under this tree, each with
# its own .git/. They are not registered as git submodules, so letting `git
# add` walk into them would embed foreign repo state incorrectly. Manage them
# in their own repos.
/Agent_backend/
/ToolSet/
Mark-XLVIII-main/tools/Orpheus-FastAPI-LMStudio/
Mark-XLVIII-main/runtime_validation/openclaw-worker/

# -----------------------------
# Claude Code local settings / runtime artifacts
# -----------------------------
# settings.local.json holds personal permission overrides (can include
# machine-specific host/path details); settings.json (shared, safe) stays
# tracked. scheduled_tasks.lock is a per-process runtime lock file.
/.claude/settings.local.json
/.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# Root-level Jarvis runtime log (distinct from the tracked Jarvis_notes/.jarvis/
# vault index) -- regenerated by .git/hooks/post-commit on every commit.
/.jarvis/*.log

# -----------------------------
# Editor / OS
# -----------------------------
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.example.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# -----------------------------
# Build artifacts and live runtime state (untracked 2026-07-31)
# -----------------------------
# These were tracked, and they rewrite on almost every run: `git status` was
# never clean, and ~75% of every byte ever committed was these files churning.
# SQLite does not delta-compress, so each commit stored a fresh whole copy of an
# 8 MB index. Packing plus untracking took .git from 87 MB to ~21 MB.
#
# All of it is regenerated automatically; nothing here is a source of truth.
#
# Note the bytecode rules at the top of this file were already present and were
# not the problem: an ignore rule does not apply to a file that is *already*
# tracked, so 144 .pyc files kept being committed for as long as they stayed in
# the index. `git rm --cached` was the missing half.

# Live vault databases -- the RAG index, model runtime state, workflow runs.
# Recreated on demand from the Markdown notes, which remain canonical.
Jarvis_notes/.jarvis/*.sqlite
Jarvis_notes/.jarvis/*.sqlite3
Jarvis_notes/.jarvis/*.db
# ...but keep recorded eval evidence and migration backups, which do not churn
# and are the only copy of what a past run actually did.
!Jarvis_notes/.jarvis/evals/**
!Jarvis_notes/.jarvis/backups/**
# The negation above re-includes whole directories, which pulled bytecode from
# the demo project inside an eval artifact back in. Evidence of what a run did,
# yes; the .pyc files it happened to leave behind, no. Placed after the negation
# so it wins.
Jarvis_notes/.jarvis/evals/**/__pycache__/

# Aletheia operator runtime state (queue, control plane, chroma index)
Mark-XLVIII-main/.aletheia_operator/

# Rotating service logs
Mark-XLVIII-main/runtime_logs/

# Generated whole-tree file inventory (7 MB of paths, sizes and SHA-1s).
# Regenerated by the scanning tooling; not referenced by any code.
/file_map.csv
